# CODEOWNERS — reviewed-lane ownership for the auto-merge lane recipe.
#
# Enable "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection. Paths listed
# here with an owner require owner approval before merge (the reviewed lane).
# Trailing entries with NO owner CLEAR ownership, so those paths need no review
# and ride the auto-merge lane. CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins, so the unowned
# auto-merge block must come AFTER the reviewed-lane entries.
#
# These patterns mirror the classifier's supported directories and depths.
# CODEOWNERS cannot express filename grammar or Git type/mode changes, so the
# canonical classifier remains authoritative when ARC arms auto-merge.
# Authoritative transition history remains owned by the catch-all, as does the
# rest of /.arc/system/.internal/.
#
# Replace @your-org/reviewers with your reviewers (a user or team).

# --- Reviewed lane: all code + constitutional docs (review required) -------
* @your-org/reviewers

# Constitutional surfaces, called out explicitly so they stay reviewed even if
# the catch-all above is later narrowed.
/.arc/system/rules/DEV-RULES.* @your-org/reviewers
/.arc/reference/adr/ @your-org/reviewers
/.arc/reference/strategies/ @your-org/reviewers

# --- Auto-merge lane: per-WU / per-cohort planning artifacts (UNOWNED) ------
# No owner on these lines clears the catch-all above, so these paths merge once
# `merge-ok` is green, with no required review. Keep this block LAST.
#
# Scoped by artifact PREFIX, NOT all of backlog/ — so shared inboxes keep the
# catch-all owner and stay reviewed. The exact generated ROADMAP is planning;
# other derived or shared backlog paths are not.
